.TH BNANO 1 "2026-08-14" "bedit 0.1.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
bnano \- edit files and write tracked changes into the bedit repository
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bnano
.I FILE
.RI [ FILE ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B bnano
launches
.B nano
for the supplied file targets. Before editing, it snapshots the current file
payload into the bedit repository. After editing, it stores a unified diff and
an access record when the file changed.
.PP
The repository location follows the same rules as
.BR bedit (1):
.B BEDIT_HOME
overrides the default home directory, and the rc file is read from
.I $BEDIT_HOME/.bedit
when that environment variable is present.
.PP
These shims accept file targets only. Repository inspection commands belong to
.BR bedit (1).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bedit (1)
